परि-√ तप् P. -तपति (fut. -तपिष्यति, MBh.; -तप्स्यति, R.; ind.p. -त॑प्य, RV.),
to burn all round, set on fire, kindle;
to feel or suffer pain;
 (with तपस्) to undergo penance, practise austerities, RV. &c. &c.:
Pass. -तप्यते (˚ति), to be purified (as by fire), Sarvad.;
to feel or suffer pain, do penance, practise austerities, MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. -तापयति, to scorch, cause great pain, torment, R.; Pañc.; Hit.

परि-√ त्यज् P. -त्यजति (˚ते, R.; MārkP.; ind.p. -त्यज्य),
to leave, quit, abandon, give up, reject, disregard, not heed, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
 (with देहम्) to forsake the body i.e. die, BhP.;
 (with प्राणान्, or जीवितम्) to resign the breath, give up the ghost, Mn.; MBh.; Daś.; Vet.;
 (with नावम्) to disembark, MW. :
Pass. -त्यज्यते, to be deprived or bereft of (instr.), Mn.; Pañc.; Hit. &c.:
Caus. -त्याजयति, to deprive or rob a person of (2 acc.), R.
